 - **Dev dependency added.** `flake8` in `requirements-devel.in`; `requirements-devel.txt` regenerated with `pip-compile` without `--upgrade` (only additions: flake8, mccabe, pycodestyle, pyflakes).
 - **Secret in tracked code, not changed.** `settings/common.py:249` holds a hard-coded `SECRET_KEY`. See the TODO in `AGENTS.md` and the `blocked` list of the harness build.
 
+## 2026-11-02: GitHub importer copies inline images into Taiga
+
+- **What changed.** `GithubImporter._import_inline_images` (`taiga/importers/github/importer.py`) finds the `https://github.com/user-attachments/assets/<id>` images of a description (markdown and `<img>` forms), asks GitHub to render each one to get a signed URL, downloads it, stores it as an `Attachment` of the user story or issue and rewrites the URL to `<attachment url>#_taiga-refresh=<type>:<id>`. Each distinct URL is imported once. A failed image (render, download, non-image Content-Type, save) keeps its GitHub link and logs a warning. `_import_user_stories_data` and `_import_issues_data` call it after the object is created and update the description only if it changed. Tests: `tests/integration/test_importers_github_inline_images.py`.
+- **What I learned.** `UserStoryStatus` and `IssueStatus` slugs come from the name, so factories need `name="open"` to get the slug `open`. `make test` calls `make db-up`, which fails with "port is already allocated" when another worktree's compose Postgres already uses 5432. All worktrees then share one server and the same `test_taiga` database, so parallel `--create-db` runs can break each other. I ran the full suite with a temporary settings module that sets another `DATABASES["default"]["TEST"]["NAME"]`.
+- **What is left.** Images in comments are not imported (comments go through `take_snapshot` with the raw GitHub body). Images are fetched one after the other, with two HTTP calls per image, so large imports get slower.
+
 ## 2026-11-01: fast gate output shows the test run
 
 - **What changed.** `make test-unit` (used by `make check-fast`) ran `pytest tests/unit --reuse-db -q`. The `-q` flag hides the pytest header ("test session starts", "collected N items") and the file names, so the harness verifier reported that the fast gate ran no tests, although 238 tests passed. The target now runs `pytest tests/unit --reuse-db -rA --tb=short`: the output shows the header, one line per test file, one `PASSED <test id>` line per test and the final summary (`238 passed`). No test or check was removed.
